dn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" class="img" alt="A Swiss glacier shows the effects of years of ice loss, with exposed rock replacing ice that once covered the landscape." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A Swiss glacier shows the effects of years of ice loss, with exposed rock replacing ice that once covered the landscape.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Swiss Academy of Natural Sciences                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Switzerland's glaciers &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5981403/swiss-glaciers-climate-change" target="_blank"&gt;lost more than 5% of their ice&lt;/a&gt; in 2026, another stark year in a long-running decline driven by global warming.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A year after the $7,500 federal EV tax credit disappeared, here's how electric and hybrid vehicles &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5979915/ev-hybrid-sales-2026-federal-tax-credit" target="_blank"&gt;have fared in the market&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Postcard from Damascus: NPR's Emily Feng &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5983516/damascus-syria-glass" target="_blank"&gt;visits a glassmaker&lt;/a&gt; working through Syria's punishing summer heat.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1155154221/majd-al-waheidi"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Majd Al-Waheidi&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; contributed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
