w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fc2%2F64%2Fd25c89dd4cc499cfe858f1acaf0a%2Fseptember-games.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fc2%2F64%2Fd25c89dd4cc499cfe858f1acaf0a%2Fseptember-games.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fc2%2F64%2Fd25c89dd4cc499cfe858f1acaf0a%2Fseptember-games.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fc2%2F64%2Fd25c89dd4cc499cfe858f1acaf0a%2Fseptember-games.jpg" class="img" alt="Silent Hill: Townfall, Control Resonant, and Fire Emblem: Fortune&amp;#039;s Weave" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 &lt;em&gt;Silent Hill: Townfall&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Control Resonant&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Fire Emblem: Fortune's Weave&lt;/em&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Konami, Remedy Entertainment, Nintendo                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;🍿 &lt;strong&gt;Movies&lt;/strong&gt;: Documentary films can often get lost in the shuffle when talking about upcoming films. &lt;em&gt;Pop Culture Happy Hour &lt;/em&gt;highlights &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/21/nx-s1-5973163/great-documentaries-you-dont-want-to-miss" target="_blank"&gt;new documentaries worth checking out&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;📺 &lt;strong&gt;TV&lt;/strong&gt;: In a new HBO docuseries, Jay-Z &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5978769/jay-z-in-8-is-a-frictionless-annotation-of-jay-zs-legacy" target="_blank"&gt;dissects his catalog&lt;/a&gt; with producer Rick Rubin. The series hopes to further cement the artist's legacy as one of the most revered lyricists of our time.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;📚 &lt;strong&gt;Books:&lt;/strong&gt; New DNA analysis has added evidence that Thomas Jefferson fathered children with Sally Hemings, a woman whom he held in slavery. The twists and turns of the investigation are detailed in a new book, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/22/nx-s1-5791513/thomas-jefferson-sally-hemings-dna-hair-smithsonian" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;History by a Hair&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;🎵 &lt;strong&gt;Music&lt;/strong&gt;: Ella Langley's "Choosin Texas" is now the longest-running No. 1 Billboard hit of all time. NPR's Stephen Thompson breaks down five reasons it's had &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/22/nx-s1-5977962/choosin-texas-ella-langley-chart-success" target="_blank"&gt;so much staying power&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;🍟 &lt;strong&gt;Food&lt;/strong&gt;: Longtime friends Brian Landry and Peter Harris have known each other since the 5th grade. The chef and jazz musician have teamed up on a new cookbook&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/20/nx-s1-5940782/cookbook-rhythm-and-roux-brian-landry-peter-harris" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;, Rhythm &amp; Roux: The Simmer and Swing of New Orleans&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, that pays tribute to two of the Big Easy's staples.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;🎮 &lt;strong&gt;Gaming&lt;/strong&gt;: Game publishers are rushing to debut their work before Grand Theft Auto 6's release in November. Here are some of &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/22/nx-s1-5971441/review-control-resonant-silent-hill-best-biggest-september-games" target="_blank"&gt;the best and biggest games&lt;/a&gt; of September.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;❓&lt;strong&gt;Quiz&lt;/strong&gt;: Stop! If you want to give yourself the best chance of acing &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/25/g-s1-144665/trump-arch-fat-bear-media-ai-news-quiz" target="_blank"&gt;this week's news quiz&lt;/a&gt;, you'll want to make sure you read the rest of this newsletter before taking it.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-144858" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5000;         --source-height: 2813;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fc6%2F16a9d0f64a8e8f6dd677cb836654%2Fgettyimages-2295245922.jpg" class="img" alt="A campaign poster urges Swiss voters to reject a neutrality initiative ahead of a Sept. 27 nationwide vote on whether to enshrine permanent armed neutrality in the constitution and limit participation in military alliances and sanctions." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A campaign poster urges Swiss voters to reject a neutrality initiative ahead of a Sept. 27 nationwide vote on whether to enshrine permanent armed neutrality in the constitution and limit participation in military alliances and sanctions.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Fabrice Coffrini/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;The people of Switzerland &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/25/nx-s1-5978905/swiss-referendum-neutrality-russia" target="_blank"&gt;will vote this weekend&lt;/a&gt; on whether to make the country's historic neutrality stance even more legally binding.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Online retailer eBay has joined its competitors in &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5978124/ebay-bans-airbags-faulty-counterfeit-auto-parts" target="_blank"&gt;banning sales of airbags&lt;/a&gt;. Earlier this year, federal regulators found that substandard airbag inflators imported from China were linked to a dozen deaths or injuries since 2023.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Star Wars &lt;/em&gt;creator George Lucas &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/23/nx-s1-5939877/george-lucas-museum-los-angeles-opening" target="_blank"&gt;opened the Lucas Museum of Narrative Art&lt;/a&gt; this week in Los Angeles. Only a small part of the museum is dedicated to his film franchise; Lucas has been collecting art since his college days.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1155154221/majd-al-waheidi"target="_blank"   &gt;Majd Al-Waheidi&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/g-s1-9395/brittney-melton"target="_blank"   &gt;Brittney Melton&lt;/a&gt; contributed.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
