" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7008x3942+0+365/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd0%2Fe5%2Fa77316e045bf85a175c6a671f00e%2Ffisherfolk-4.jpg" class="img" alt="Pavadairayan, 60, a migrant laborer known as a “basket man,” carries fish from boats to the auction house at Kasimedu Fishing Harbour in Chennai, India." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Pavadairayan, 60, a migrant laborer known as a "basket man," carries fish from boats to the auction house at Kasimedu Fishing Harbour in Chennai, India.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Viraj Nayar                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In the heart of Chennai, India, the Kasimedu Fishing Harbour serves as a makeshift market where residents battle the sea for survival and a wage. Basket men, carrying around 35 pounds of fish on their heads, make 40 to 50 trips to the daily auction during long shifts. They're joined by fishermen, auctioneers, fish hawkers and wholesalers, transport workers and ice suppliers. The harbor, originally built for fewer than 600 boats, now serves more than 1,000. Bhagat Singh, a researcher and social worker, says that members of the fishing community understand the risks of the business. Fishermen there earn about $200 a month if they have good catches, but one bad season could potentially plunge them into poverty. This precariousness of the career path is driving younger generations to seek more reliable employment. Check out these &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/20/g-s1-143447/photos-fishermen-sea-india" target="_blank"&gt;photos of the lives of these fisherfolk&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143800" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2600;         --source-height: 1463;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+907/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F95%2Fed%2F26fff5d24a89bf8c200320ae302b%2Fimage-13.jpg" class="img" alt="Rose Friedman came to NPR in 2010. She was an editor for the Society &amp;amp; Culture desk." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Rose Friedman came to NPR in 2010. She was an editor for the Society &amp; Culture desk.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Beth Novey/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rose Friedman, an influential editor and reporter at NPR for 15 years, has &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/18/nx-s1-5973098/rose-friedman-dies" target="_blank"&gt;died from cancer at the age of 38&lt;/a&gt;. She co-created the popular annual &lt;em&gt;Books We Love&lt;/em&gt; reading guide.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A judge has ordered Fox Corp. to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/20/nx-s1-5974900/fox-shareholders-murdoch-lawsuit" target="_blank"&gt;hand over hundreds of documents&lt;/a&gt; that could reveal how founder Rupert Murdoch managed some of his media companies' most significant scandals over the past two decades.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Florida citrus growers are &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/18/nx-s1-5966501/trees-gene-editing-florida-citrus-industry" target="_blank"&gt;planting trees with gene-editing technology&lt;/a&gt; to combat the deadly citrus greening disease that has devastated many of their crops.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
